  "_comment": "English plurals, both ways. wishbuilder/English (Java) and tools/english.py read this one file, and EnglishTest + tools/english.py sync hold them equal over every installed name. plural: what the rules (y -> ies, s/x/z/ch/sh -> es, else s) get wrong, singular -> plural. suffixes: a word ENDING in the key takes the value ('enderman' -> 'endermen'). reading: a plural a child types -> the word it is read as; a plural that is also a verb is left out ('leaves', 'lives', 'goes'). same: the plural is the word. mass: a material, said '16 dirt' (items only; a creature always takes a plural). already: a head word that is already plural ('Sweet Berries', 'Oak Planks'): said 'some oak planks' for one. pair: of those, the ones said 'a pair of shears'. proper: a one-word name said as it is, with no article ('Moddy'). names: whole names the rules cannot say. breaks: the head word is the word before the first of these ('Eyes of Ender', 'Boats with Chest', 'Carrots on a Stick').",
